Here are the main ones for the network editor (hover over the network pane so it has focus):

Moving through the hierarchy

U: go up one level, to the parent network
I: dive into the selected COMP
Alt+Left / Alt+Right: step back and forward through your previous network locations, like a browser history (I'm less certain of this one, so check it in Help > Shortcuts)

Viewing, scaling and recentering

H: Home, which fits all nodes in the current network to the pane
Shift+H: Home Selected, which frames only the selected nodes
Mouse wheel: zoom in and out around the cursor
Middle-mouse drag: pan around the network

Useful nearby

Tab: open the operator create menu
P: toggle the parameter dialog for the selected node
A: toggle the live viewer on the selected node, so you can see its output inside the node
Ctrl+F: find operators in the network

Mac users swap Ctrl for Cmd where relevant. The full list is under Help > Shortcuts, and the TouchDesigner wiki has a "Shortcuts" page if you want the complete reference.
